Module Std.IOUtils
Use Std.Files

== Functions on text files and the file system (canon r3.58 module pair;
== OpenSpec change file-io). They are compiler intrinsics, visible in a
== program that uses Std.IOUtils, so their names stay free elsewhere.
==
== Opening (F2) — a new File, owned by the variable that receives it:
==   OpenRead(Path String) File      == an existing file, for reading
==   Create(Path String) File        == a new or truncated file, for writing
==   OpenAppend(Path String) File    == a new or existing file, writing at its end
==
== Text (F4, F5) — UTF-8; lines end with "\n" when written, and "\n" or
== "\r\n" are accepted when read:
==   ReadLn(F File) String           == the next line without its line end; "" at the end
==   Eof(F File) Bool                == true when nothing is left to read
==   Write(F File, Values...)        == the values, as Put prints them
==   WriteLn(F File, Values...)      == the values and one line end, as PutLn
==   Close(F File)                   == flush and close now (also automatic)
==
== File system (F7):
==   Exists(Path String) Bool        == a regular file exists at Path
==   DeleteFile(Path String)         == delete a file (never a directory)
==   RenameFile(From String, To String)  == AlreadyExists when To exists
==
== Every failure raises FileNotFound, PermissionDenied, AlreadyExists,
== DiskFull or IOError (Std.Errors), handled with try, except On, Else,
== ensure and Retry like any exception:
==
==   try
==       F := OpenRead("dados.txt")
==       while not Eof(F)
==           PutLn(ReadLn(F))
==       ;
==   except
==       On FileNotFound
==           PutLn("dados.txt não existe")
==       ;
==   ensure
==       PutLn("fim")
==   ;
